# The folder above ignores every PNG and names its exceptions one at a time,
# because the default capture writes six frames nobody asked for and an
# untracked file there fails the gate's tree-clean step for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the push. The same rule applies here, and it lands on the
# same split docs/frames/effect-candidates/.gitignore lands on: which framing
# decides.
#
# THE WIDE FRAME IS THE ONLY ONE THERE IS, AND IT IS COMMITTED. Issue #270
# settled that a sheet and the built player disagree, so a candidate that is not
# read at 1600x900 has not been read -- and played/ is where that reading
# happens. The other half of the pair issue #270 asks for is not a second camera
# on this board; it is the -Width 28 sheet under docs/frames/roster, for the
# reason the block below gives.
#
# THE WHOLE FOLDER IS TEMPORARY. It is the set of alternatives #284 signs from,
# and it goes when the signing does.
#
#   ./tools/capture-rung-candidates.ps1                redraws everything
!played/*.png

# THERE IS NO close/ HERE, unlike in effect-candidates. Every candidate was
# drawn at a close distance first and the pass answered nothing: OrbitCameraRig
# frames the whole board and -Distance crops toward its middle, so the five rows
# this defense stands -- which are in the top-left corner -- fall outside the
# closer frame, and all four Mortar candidates came back byte-identical to each
# other. README.md carries the whole of it. The magnified view of these
# questions is a sheet under docs/frames/roster instead.
close/
